From 69a7192012a28eae04c708cfa35edc889936f697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:13:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] esp32s3: unmapping one view of a flash page leaves its
 other views alone

The MMU model holds flash in one buffer by physical address, shared by
every virtual page that maps it, and filled a page with 0xdeadbeef when
an entry mapping it was invalidated. A flash page can be mapped twice:
ESP-IDF's esp_image_verify() (behind Arduino's ESP.getSketchSize() and
getSketchMD5(), and OTA) maps the running app's own pages to read them,
then unmaps them, and the running code and its literals turned into
0xdeadbeef: the next l32r jumped there, and the panic handler overflowed
the main task's stack. Every Arduino-ESP32 3.x sketch that sized or hashed
itself, and SlimeVR's tracker firmware at boot, died this way.

Clear a page only when no other valid entry still maps it, and never for
an entry that was already invalid (its page number is stale: often 0).

esp32s3-mmu-test maps one page at two virtual pages and unmaps one; it
read 0xdeadbeef through the other before this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sb26stwPJiCMHhrBWZ2D9q
